<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Henry Dundas</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1742">1742</a>–<a href="/years/1811">1811</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> · Also known as Henry Dundas, 1st Viscount Melville</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Henry Dundas, later 1st Viscount Melville, was a Scottish lawyer and politician who dominated the management of Scottish politics for about three decades in the late eighteenth century. A close ally of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/william-pitt-the-younger">William Pitt the Younger</a>, he presided over the Board of Control for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a> and served as Secretary of State for War. In 1806 he was impeached for misuse of naval funds and acquitted.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/henry-dundas.jpg" alt="Henry Dundas" width="320" height="386" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Thomas Lawrence · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Henry_Dundas,_1st_Viscount_Melville_by_Sir_Thomas_Lawrence.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
